  "content": {
    "id": "v2-1cf69-p14-practice-slot-2-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": null,
    "prompt": "Solve these trigonometric equations for $x\\in[0,2\\pi)$ by squaring both sides.",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "v2-1cf69-p14-practice-slot-2-slot-2-q-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$\\sin x+\\cos x=1$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=0,\\frac{\\pi}{2}$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}(\\sin x+\\cos x)^2&=1\\\\1+2\\sin x\\cos x&=1\\\\\\sin2x&=0\\end{align*}$$\nLet $u=2x$, so $0\\le u<4\\pi$. Then $u=0,\\pi,2\\pi,3\\pi$, so $x=0,\\frac{\\pi}{2},\\pi,\\frac{3\\pi}{2}$.\nCheck in $\\sin x+\\cos x=1$:\n$x=0$: $0+1=1$ ✓\n$x=\\frac{\\pi}{2}$: $1+0=1$ ✓\n$x=\\pi$: $0-1=-1$ ✗\n$x=\\frac{3\\pi}{2}$: $-1+0=-1$ ✗\nTherefore $x=0$ or $\\frac{\\pi}{2}$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 60
      },
      {
        "id": "v2-1cf69-p14-practice-slot-2-slot-2-q-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$\\sin x+\\cos x=\\sqrt2$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=\\frac{\\pi}{4}$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}(\\sin x+\\cos x)^2&=2\\\\1+2\\sin x\\cos x&=2\\\\\\sin2x&=1\\end{align*}$$\nLet $u=2x$, so $0\\le u<4\\pi$. Then $u=\\frac{\\pi}{2},\\frac{5\\pi}{2}$, so $x=\\frac{\\pi}{4},\\frac{5\\pi}{4}$.\nCheck in $\\sin x+\\cos x=\\sqrt2$:\n$x=\\frac{\\pi}{4}$: $\\frac{\\sqrt2}{2}+\\frac{\\sqrt2}{2}=\\sqrt2$ ✓\n$x=\\frac{5\\pi}{4}$: $-\\frac{\\sqrt2}{2}-\\frac{\\sqrt2}{2}=-\\sqrt2$ ✗\nTherefore $x=\\frac{\\pi}{4}$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 60
      }
    ]
  },
